!-----------------------------------------------------------------------
!
! Cross-section data for : HO2 + hv --> OH + O
! quantum yield set ARBITRARILY to 1 !
! Orig data found in ./in/crs_ho2.dat
! 190nm - 260nm : JPL2006 (no update since JPL-2002):
! 	http://www.atmosphere.mpg.de/enid/2295(catalogue -> Peroxy radicals -> Hydroperoxy HO2 -> JPL-2002(2002)
! 	Rem1: With respect to the crs2004 file (crs provided by JPL-1997), the wavelength range has been extended from 190-250nm to 190-260nm.
!		The wl step has also been reduced from 10nm to 5nm.
!	Rem2: JPL-2006 reported a study showing the production of O1D at 193nm and 248nm, with a quantum yield that is about 15 times larger
!       	at the longer wl. The absolute q.y. for O1D production has not been reported yet.
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Begins at wl interval :        55  | Finishes at wl interval :   82
